# USDA FoodData Central key — free: https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
# Copy to .env (gitignored). Leaving it blank is fine for `npm run food`, which
# falls back to DEMO_KEY at 30 requests/hour — about five searches, since each
# result row costs a request. Everything else refuses to run without a real key.
#
# Keep private. USDA deactivates published keys, and this must never become an
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* var — Expo inlines those into the app bundle. Calling FDC from
# the app needs a server-side proxy that injects this key.
FDC_API_KEY=

# Supabase, for the app. Both of these are the opposite case to the key above:
# they are *designed* to ship inside the bundle, which is what EXPO_PUBLIC_ does.
# Auth and RLS protect the data, not the secrecy of these strings. Copy the real
# values from Project Settings → API Keys; use the publishable key
# (`sb_publishable_…`), not the legacy anon JWT, which is compatibility-only.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
